  "uuid": "d182a026-7c29-4f66-a90c-8895a207aa90",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "2e0f6e99-894f-07af-2198-20025af9cf59",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "6accbb34-b8d3-0161-96cb-f25b94080171",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"The knowledge that trained cancer nurses have is really critical,\" Assistant Professor Tayreez Mushani said. \"They can detect breast cancer early through manual exams. They can safely administer chemotherapy and other treatments. They can manage side effects and counsel patients so they feel comfortable continuing their treatment.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In addition to working with patients at the bedside, graduates will be leaders who expand access to skilled cancer care. For example, Immaculate Wambugu has been asked to establish an oncology nursing training programme at Nairobi Hospital's Cicely McDonell College of Health Science after she graduates. \"I think the course is a very good thing for our country,\" Wambugu said. \"I want to help more people get this kind of training.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The Princess Margaret Cancer Centre of Toronto played an essential role in developing the Diploma in Oncology Nursing at AKU in Nairobi and Moi. The Centre initially reached out to the University about collaborating to train cancer nurses, and helped to develop the diploma curriculum.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The Centre also supports Mushani in her work and in assisting faculty at Moi. \"A cancer diagnosis changes your life,\" said Pamela Savage, Director of Professional Practice at Princess Margaret. \"East Africa needs nurses who can address the challenges patients face.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
